From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sargo@sargo.cc>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 11:23:47 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 09/15] Plutonium: tab features: permissions, downloads, file
 pickers, printing and more

What tabs need from a desktop, asked of the shell: permission prompts and per-thread grants, downloads, file pickers, printing, page zoom, find in page, context menus, media sessions over MPRIS, speechSynthesis voices; pages see Linux, not ChromeOS.

It holds these changes:
- Chrome's own UI in the shell (DevTools, context menus, keys)
- page zoom for tabs
- find in page for tabs
- tabs' permission prompts ask the shell
- per-thread permission grants
- downloads for the shells' tabs
- file pickers for tabs ask the shell
- printing in tabs goes to the shell
- a folder upload the shell confirmed skips Chrome's dialog
- pages see Linux, not ChromeOS
- only the shell window is held fullscreen
- tabs' media sessions over MPRIS
- speechSynthesis voices from speech-dispatcher

and the parts in these files of:
- shell mode on DRM, evdev input fix, display-plane path
- native fullscreen for embedded apps and tabs, Super+F, shell shortcuts
- several live shells, Super+Tab switches between them
- Google sign-in on the web; tabs fullscreen outside the shells
- a tab's context menu item runs with the tab focused
- no Ash toasts, nudges or clipboard history, no Chrome toasts or clipboard bubble over the shell
